# {{ .ProviderName }}

A Crossplane provider for managing cloud resources.

## Getting Started

### Install Provider

Apply a `Provider` package pointing at your built (and pushed) image:

```yaml
apiVersion: pkg.crossplane.io/v1
kind: Provider
metadata:
  name: {{ .ProviderName }}
spec:
  package: {{ .Repo }}:latest
```

For local development without building or pushing an image, use `make dev`
instead (see Development below) — it creates a kind cluster with your CRDs
installed and runs the controller from source.

### Configure Provider

Apply a ProviderConfig and its credentials:

```bash
kubectl apply -f examples/provider/config.yaml
```

## Development

### Build

Run `make` to build the provider:

```bash
make
```

### Test

Run tests with:

```bash
make test
```

### Deploy

For local development without building or pushing an image, use `make dev`
(see above). For a full end-to-end run — package, deploy via Crossplane, and
run the uptest/chainsaw suites — use:

```bash
make e2e
```